WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
This is the practical setup.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.880
The website explains MOMM.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.960
The Setup Center connects your tools.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.920
The ledger records your reviews.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.520
Three different jobs.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.600
Let's get your first reviewer ready.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.580
Open the installation guide.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.180
Copy the install or upgrade prompt into the agent you use.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.780
It checks Git, Node eighteen or newer, your existing installation,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.080
and the published stable release.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.080
Choose a permanent folder outside your projects.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.080
Review the plan, then approve it.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.020
You don't need every harness, or every reviewer.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.020
Ask your agent to open MOMM's Setup Center.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.989
If you prefer the terminal, run the setup command from the skills

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:39.320
clone.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.047
The address is local to your machine, and its port may differ from

00:00:43.047 --> 00:00:43.620
this recording.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.300
Don't paste somebody else's localhost address and expect their

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:48.820
dashboard.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.280
Choose your current agent as the governor.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.220
That's the agent writing and testing your work.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.600
It is excluded from reviewing itself.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.780
Now pick an external reviewer.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.800
One is enough to begin.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.080
Add more when another perspective is worth the extra quota.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.260
An installed command line tool is not the same as a working account.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.024
Use its official login action and complete the browser login

00:01:12.024 --> 00:01:12.400
yourself.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.840
No API keys.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.460
Then verify the connection.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.448
Quick Setup tests detected sessions using a disclosed synthetic

00:01:19.448 --> 00:01:21.220
sentence, not your project.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.271
A successful check is evidence for now, not a promise about every

00:01:24.271 --> 00:01:24.780
future review.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.456
The maintenance panel separates installed versions from update

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:30.040
availability.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.220
Check first.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.020
Read the proposed change.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.860
Run an update only when you choose to.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:39.769
MOMM's own signed updates also protect protocol changes with explicit

00:01:39.769 --> 00:01:40.160
acceptance.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.710
If you update MOMM, relaunch Setup Center so you're not looking at an

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:45.760
older running page.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.000
Follow the actual status.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.660
Missing means install the official tool.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.780
Authentication required means complete its login.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.520
Provider unavailable means wait and retry, not re-login.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.100
Quota exhausted means deal with the provider's allowance.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.307
You can continue with another ready reviewer; don't turn a failed

00:02:04.307 --> 00:02:06.640
route into a successful one on the screen.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.180
Back in your project, approve which providers may receive the work.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.600
Ask MOMM to review your changes, investigate material findings,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.780
verify fixes, record every decision, and give you the ledger link.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.048
That completes the journey: set up once, request a review, then

00:02:23.048 --> 00:02:24.212
check what happened.
